WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.520
You really don't want to come back with me?

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.520
I'll take you to the Forbidden 
Library, as promised.

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:11.740
Right now I am more preoccupied with 
my ducklings than <i>The Grimoire of Zero</i>.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.460
They grow dramatically
 before one knows it.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.030
I can't take my eyes off them.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.790
Well, to you, a few years 
is like the blink of an eye.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.600
True.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.520
I didn't see thee for a short 
time and thou hast grown old.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.050
The next time I see thee, 
thou mightest be dead of old age.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.800
I always look young and spry!

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.440
You got your memories back?!

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.590
Yeah. But they're not very good memories.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.020
Do you wanna forget again? 
Want a smack to the head?

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.410
No thanks.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.160
But it barely feels like I remembered.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.400
I thought things would be 
different once I remembered.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.290
But I still know nothing...

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.040
What do you mean?

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:14.890
What is it like to have
 feelings for someone?

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:15.550
Huh?!

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.470
Professor Los says that 
you're in love with me.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.720
What?! Um...

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.570
I...

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.190
I was wondering what normally 
happens when you like someone.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:35.820
Well... you want to be 
special to them, I guess...

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:39.290
You <i>are</i> special to me, Hort.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.750
Is this love?

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:42.330
What?

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:48.080
No. I don't think it is.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.210
Oh. Sorry.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.150
It's okay!

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:55.710
I'm happy you're asking 
me for love advice, Sayb!

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.880
Oh, how about this.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.720
Who comes to mind when 
you think you might die?

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.220
When I think I might die?

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:09.850
Oh...

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.690
I think I might like Professor Los.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:21.340
I get that.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.660
I adore Professor Los, too!

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:29.260
You can always talk to me, so promise me!

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.820
That you'll come to me for love advice first!

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:36.420
Th-Thanks.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:40.130
I wish there were something 
I could do for you, too.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:43.820
How about a morning magic supply?
 Is that okay?

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.760
Thanks!

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:46.480
Sure.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:58.790
I can't!

00:02:58.790 --> 00:02:59.390
What?

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.420
Sorry, Hort.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.970
I need to go see Professor Zero.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:53.390
Episode 9     A Stone Cast Into the Pond

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.710
<i>I think I might like Professor Los.</i>

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.980
Yes! I shall pretend I never heard that!

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.480
Professor Los! Professor Los!

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:05.900
Sayb says he likes you!

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:10.240
P-Professor Los?

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:19.900
Hort, one should not go around blabbing 
someone else's feelings to others.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.480
Professor Zero,

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.520
I, um...

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:36.180
Sit down, young man.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.900
Then we can talk.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:43.360
Professor Los, you won't leave us, will you?

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.030
Why dost thou ask that?

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:49.540
'Cause teachers run when a 
student falls for them, right?

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.490
Since it's a burden and a pain.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:56.910
I know, because something like 
that happened at the Church!

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:02.260
I should like to dissemble, 
but I am fond of keen insight.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:06.630
Just as thou fearest, 
I am the type of teacher who runs.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.480
No! Please, no!

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.370
I don't want you to leave, Professor!

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:17.640
And it would be so sad for Sayb, too, 
if the person he likes disappears!

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:22.110
That's why I was going to pretend 
not to have heard anything...

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:27.960
Worry not. I have yet to 
tire of observing you three.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:35.240
It happened sooner than I expected.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.500
And your reaction is calmer 
than I feared it would be.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.400
But I was frantic when I got here.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.340
True, you were.

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:47.550
But you weren't trembling with fear,

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.420
nor were you a captive of despair.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:54.050
You have gained the strength not 
to be crushed by your memories.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:57.020
Crushed by my memories?

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:02.960
Unpleasant memories can at times become a 
poison that eats away at you from the inside.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:11.240
Why did I suddenly remember?

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.680
I imagine because your life was in danger.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.210
In other words, you sought to live.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:22.620
Young man, you are no longer empty.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:28.300
You sought a way to fight, even if it meant 
dredging up painful memories.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.880
My mother told me something.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.690
She said never approach a 
witch with eyes like mine.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.890
These eyes are somewhat special.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:44.420
They are something my brother 
and I inherited from our father.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:50.610
And that brother is your father, Thirteen.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:08:00.380
Thirteen and I are each other's 
last remaining brethren.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:07.380
Perhaps that's why he would have done 
anything for me, even destroy the world.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:10.180
Your magic is part of that.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:13.540
He plotted for it all to be offered up to me.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:18.320
He must have realized that if his 
blood and your mother's combined,

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:21.990
he would obtain a child with limitless magic.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:26.100
Your mother caught on and fled.

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:31.490
So then... you're...

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:33.710
That makes me your aunt.

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:37.120
So there's not really 
any danger. Isn't that right?

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:41.250
Even so, most of the pain you've 
experienced is my fault.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:45.230
It may have been because of you, 
but that doesn't mean it was your fault.

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:51.950
Besides. If not for you, 
Professor Zero, I would not exist.

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:55.360
You take after him.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.660
After my father?

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:01.470
Only in the good aspects, I mean.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.920
I want to hear about my father.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.730
Or, I mean, I want to know.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.580
To know just who I am...

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.920
Your father was a thorough rationalist.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:16.510
If it was rational,

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:19.450
he could even work with someone who 
was a mortal enemy moments earlier.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:23.950
But rationality at times leads to cruelty.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:31.710
As a result of his extreme rationalism, 
he committed a grave, irreparable misdeed.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.780
The war.

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:38.560
To obtain a world for witches, 
Thirteen sacrificed countless lives.

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:41.260
An evil sorcerer whose name 
will go down in history.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:44.430
That is my brother, your father.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:49.940
I feel like I know a little 
better what I want to be.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:55.690
This morning I went to supply Hort 
with magic, but I couldn't do it.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:10:00.180
I felt like I might kill Hort, 
and I got scared.

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:02.840
I see.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:06.070
But I want to keep being a magic supplier,

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:10.040
at least during the field program.

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:12.020
For your friends?

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:14.280
For me.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:18.260
Hort and Kudo are going to 
teach me magic in exchange.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.970
So please let me practice on you, Professor.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:24.340
Since even if I mess up, 
you won't die.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:29.480
What? Both hands?

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:32.990
We'll circulate magic between us.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:36.340
Keep adjusting so the amount stays constant.

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:45.870
Kudo!

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.250
Be calm. Don't break your concentration.

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:52.910
Sorcery and magic require concentration.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:57.490
If you stop your incantation every 
time a comrade screams in combat,

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:59.220
you'll lose people you could have saved.

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:00.420
But...

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:03.470
I'll become stronger.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.860
Yes. You will indeed get stronger.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:09.520
Perhaps even stronger than I.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:11.980
My goodness.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:16.900
It seems we arrived quite a bit late.

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:24.680
Oh, thou art younger than I thought.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:29.200
Thy face was in quite a state last night.

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:34.710
What are you doing, Tyrant? Let go of him!

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:39.740
Okey dokey.

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:47.700
My dear Ludens,

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.100
say hello!

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:01.360
You think he's here on 
orders from the Church?

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:06.950
I bet so. To the Church, 
a penniless kid is just a pawn.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:12.300
There are many good-hearted 
people within the Church, too.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:17.040
I can't say I approve of 
such over-generalization.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:20.170
Ah, if it isn't Lady Hearthful!

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:23.130
Shouldst thou not be at the school?

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:25.680
I ended class in the morning today.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:29.260
I brought lunch for our patient.

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:35.250
Only, I heard a scream on the way,
 so I came to investigate.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:38.440
Please forgive me for 
essentially eavesdropping.

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:42.460
Thou hast a proper sense of 
yourself as being protected.

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:47.450
Still, lately it smells like 
trouble is brewing, does it not?

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:51.080
Dost thou not feel it is 
time to flee the village?

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:52.910
Goodness, no.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:57.920
It is to be expected that the extremists 
within the Church would target a witch village.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.640
Everyone who came here was 
prepared for that possibility.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:03.920
Whaddya want?

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:06.460
As I said, I brought you lunch.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:11.180
Oh... well, that was... kind of ya.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:14.390
This one is

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:17.620
for him.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:21.160
He is still just a kid.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:27.700
Did the extremists not consider 
that a child like him would fail?

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:29.660
Good point.

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:30.970
He is chum.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:36.060
To the anti-witch faction, 
this village is a murky swamp.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:39.150
They do not know what fish 
there might be, or how many.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:41.880
So then, he's...?

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:49.310
They probably wished to see how this young man 
would be killed for attacking with clear hostility.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.830
He'll get no sympathy from me!

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:58.520
He tried to stab not just 
me, but Professor Los, too!

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:01.940
He attacked the one he thought 
was weakest to break through.

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:05.730
He'd even have no qualms 
killing the village children.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:11.790
Ah, but, Kudo, no one said 
anything about sympathy.

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:14.360
I don't... I didn't...

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:15.690
Thou dost, right?

00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:18.290
Though dost have sympathy for him, right?

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:20.880
Very well!

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:23.920
I am fond of compassion 
that overcomes even hatred!

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.630
Here, I shall pat thee for it!

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:27.240
I'm jealous!

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:27.730
Stop it!

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:28.930
I'll show compassion, too! I will!

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.750
That is bad manners.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:32.970
Would you like to sit and eat at a table?

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.240
I'm an Arbiter, you know.

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:40.060
Even for Arbiters and witches, 
etiquette and manners are important.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.940
Oh? Am I gonna etiquette 
my enemies to death?

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:48.670
Other people's opinions of you can 
be a way of protecting yourself.

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:53.460
Manners are a useful and efficient 
way of gaining positive regard.

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:57.700
I'm only regarded for killing.

00:14:58.070 --> 00:15:04.420
You intend to build relationships with 
others in this village through killing?

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:08.210
That's my job. Ain't that right, boss?

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:12.470
Your job is protecting, not killing!

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:14.660
Ain't that the same thing?

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:16.220
Not at all!

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:22.720
Ah, yes. If your job is to protect the village,
 then you need to learn about it.

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:25.980
Might I show you around the village?

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:30.240
Huh? U-Um, I think that's 
dangerous. He's a killer.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:33.730
I ain't gonna kill anybody for free.

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:36.800
But if there's money in it, then—

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:40.720
I must inform you that 
acting fearsome like that

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:43.250
will gain you nothing here.

00:15:43.490 --> 00:15:46.630
No one in this village will fear you.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:49.900
Oh, is that so?

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:57.380
Professor Los, no need to escalate.

00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:03.260
I'm sure it was just a little test to 
see if I really wouldn't be afraid.

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:07.040
Do not play games like this again, Tyrant.

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:09.610
Next time thy head shall fly.

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:12.200
My bad.

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:16.380
Shall we go, then, Mr. Tyrant?

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.790
Hey, he's just a kid.

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:24.290
So the assailant was just some kid.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:28.290
I wanted to get some 
information out of him,

00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:30.780
but this changes the plan.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:32.800
What was the plan?

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:34.800
Torture.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:37.800
N-No torturing!

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:40.160
I'm saying I'm not gonna torture a kid.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.060
No adults, either!

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:47.240
The plan was to send him to Wenias 
once his condition is stable!

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:49.070
But <i>torture</i>?

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:51.420
That ain't the rule of law!

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:53.080
W-Wow, Kudo!

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.680
You sound super smart!

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:57.030
I agree!

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:58.320
No torture!

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.620
You're quite right.

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:03.710
If torture's out, then this 
is a job for the priest.

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:05.090
The priest?

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:08.670
True. The Father can use verbal torment—

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:09.820
Look out!

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:14.920
I'm surprised. That was intended to hit.

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:18.180
No violence! You call yourself a clergyman?

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:22.180
You never know who could be listening.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:28.190
If you grasped that better, I would 
not need to resort to violence.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.620
Also, look.

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:33.570
He's awake. Has been for a while.

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:51.670
Realize your position,

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:56.800
heretic who comprehends not a single 
ounce of the chaste Church's aims.

00:17:56.800 --> 00:18:00.300
Damn it! Is everyone in 
this village a monster?

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:02.560
What is evil?

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:04.310
Just what

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.060
is a monster?

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:11.100
If your head is for show and lacks even 
the sense an infant would retain,

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:15.570
shall I cut it off and replace it 
with the head of that monster there?

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:17.420
<i>Does he mean me?</i>

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:18.570
Yikes.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:22.080
Can the room be made dark?

00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:23.270
Indeed.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:39.590
Whoa! I-It's so dark!

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:41.710
'Tis roughly a moonlit night.

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:44.850
Perhaps a bit too bright 
for the priest's eyes.

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:46.850
No. This is enough.

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:52.360
I will ask you several questions, 
but you need not answer them.

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:55.470
If you wish to answer, I will not stop you.

00:18:55.470 --> 00:18:58.130
But if you lie, I will know.

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:08.120
Were you the only one sent to this 
village with the Remnant of Disaster?

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:10.870
Good question.

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:13.880
Affirmed. Well, as anticipated.

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:17.160
What?! I didn't say—

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:21.760
Are further attacks with 
Remnants of Disaster planned?

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:24.930
How should I know?

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:27.880
You showed signs of embarrassment.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:30.820
I see. It appears you really don't know.

00:19:30.820 --> 00:19:34.600
Furthermore, you are embarrassed 
you weren't informed.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.270
Is there a plan to rescue you?

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.280
D—

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:39.940
Strong negative.

00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:44.530
It was made clear to you that you 
would not be rescued if captured.

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:48.040
What? How does he know? Is it a bluff?

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:49.700
Facial expressions.

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:52.640
Movements of the pupils, eyelids, and lips.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:55.800
He is reading unconsciously 
expressed emotion.

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.550
He can do that?!

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:59.780
I have the general picture.

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:01.550
You may let it be light again.

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.550
To be frank,

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:08.320
we gained little information.

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:14.310
Nor can we exclude the possibility that the 
boy was supplied with false information.

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:18.480
From the fact that they acquired 
a Remnant of Destruction,

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:24.820
a higher-up at the Church is involved.
Someone fairly high up, at that.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.820
Unfortunately.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:33.080
So someone is presenting themselves as 
a peace faction, but supporting the extremists.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:37.450
The internal conflict within the 
Church is pretty messy right now, isn't it?

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.090
How alarming.

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:44.980
Someone so high up must have better 
cards to play than a powerless boy.

00:20:44.980 --> 00:20:46.090
In other words,

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:49.100
further moves ought to be coming.

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:51.560
But strangely, there has been no movement.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:55.350
What should be happening, isn't.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.100
Which means,

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:59.080
the move has already been made in secret.

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:00.360
We must assume so.

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:03.020
For now, regarding that boy,

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:07.490
it may be best to delay his 
transfer to Wenias for a bit.

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:12.230
The adults are deciding 
everything themselves.

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:17.000
I can fight, too, you know!

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:19.050
Yeah, right.

00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:22.920
A student who can't take 
responsibility can't do anything.

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:39.790
My, how rare for you to come by the school.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:44.260
I was just showing Mr. Tyrant around.

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:45.030
Oh.

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:47.200
What's that they're making?

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:49.530
He says it's a trap to catch fish.

00:21:50.020 --> 00:21:54.290
He apparently worked at a workshop 
that made traps for hunting.

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:58.300
Did he say, "traps for hunting people"?

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:59.790
Yes. First thing.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:04.800
Apparently he can't help but try to scare me.

00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:07.550
He's like a little kid.

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:10.040
Look, mister! I finished my trap!

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:16.060
I'd say this looks pretty good.

00:22:16.710 --> 00:22:19.440
Ms. Hearthful! I wanna go to the river!

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:23.570
A fine idea. Why don't we all 
go there together tomorrow?

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:25.280
Yay!

00:22:32.310 --> 00:22:36.200
I suppose the idea of us going 
alone is still a little worrisome.

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:39.040
Might I ask you to escort us?

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:41.210
O-Of course!

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:42.740
Are you coming, too, mister?

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:46.210
Depends on the boss.
 I don't get to decide.

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:48.870
Of course you're coming, too!

00:22:48.870 --> 00:22:51.340
Don't forget, you're my servant!

00:22:52.030 --> 00:22:53.090
Sure, sure.

00:22:53.090 --> 00:22:58.390
But are ya sure? You want a killer 
like me to be around kids?

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:01.310
Hey! Not in front of the children!

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:04.450
Mister, are you gonna kill us?

00:23:04.450 --> 00:23:07.240
Nah, I mean... I don't intend to.

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:11.110
Then it's fine for him to be 
around us. Right, everyone?

00:23:11.110 --> 00:23:12.940
I agree!

00:23:11.110 --> 00:23:12.940
Yeah!

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:17.080
What're ya teaching these kids?

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:18.850
As I told you.

00:23:18.850 --> 00:23:22.080
No resident of this village will fear you.

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:24.590
If there isn't sufficient reason to fear,

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:28.340
we won't be scared of anything.

00:23:42.930 --> 00:23:44.960
<i>The transfer is postponed?</i>

00:23:47.880 --> 00:23:49.200
Damn it!

00:23:49.200 --> 00:23:50.110
Hey.

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:51.610
Come with me.

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>Next Episode      "Snack Time"</b>

00:23:55.870 --> 00:23:58.290
Eating something yummy 
makes people feel better.

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:01.370
So, I'm gonna make yummy food!

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:03.370
Next episode: "Snack Time."

00:24:03.690 --> 00:24:06.290
Professor Los, you're awfully quiet.

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:09.100
No comment. Wait for next week!
